Expand description

A widget to display some text.

It is used to display a block of text. The text can be styled and aligned. It can also be wrapped to the next line if it is too long to fit in the given area.

The text can be any type that can be converted into a [`Text`](../prelude/struct.Text.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Text"). By default, the text is styled with [`Style::default()`](../prelude/struct.Style.html#method.default "associated function ratatui::prelude::Style::default"), not wrapped, and aligned to the left.

The text can be wrapped to the next line if it is too long to fit in the given area. The wrapping can be configured with the [`wrap`](struct.Paragraph.html#method.wrap "method ratatui::widgets::Paragraph::wrap") method. For more complex wrapping, consider using the [Textwrap crate](https://crates.io/crates/textwrap).

The text can be aligned to the left, right, or center. The alignment can be configured with the [`alignment`](struct.Paragraph.html#method.alignment "method ratatui::widgets::Paragraph::alignment") method or with the [`left_aligned`](struct.Paragraph.html#method.left_aligned "method ratatui::widgets::Paragraph::left_aligned"), [`right_aligned`](struct.Paragraph.html#method.right_aligned "method ratatui::widgets::Paragraph::right_aligned"), and [`centered`](struct.Paragraph.html#method.centered "method ratatui::widgets::Paragraph::centered") methods.

The text can be scrolled to show a specific part of the text. The scroll offset can be set with the [`scroll`](struct.Paragraph.html#method.scroll "method ratatui::widgets::Paragraph::scroll") method.

The text can be surrounded by a [`Block`](struct.Paragraph.html#method.block "method ratatui::widgets::Paragraph::block") with a title and borders. The block can be configured with the [`block`](struct.Paragraph.html#method.block "method ratatui::widgets::Paragraph::block") method.

The style of the text can be set with the [`style`](struct.Paragraph.html#method.style "method ratatui::widgets::Paragraph::style") method. This style will be applied to the entire widget, including the block if one is present. Any style set on the block or text will be added to this style. See the [`Style`](struct.Paragraph.html#method.style "method ratatui::widgets::Paragraph::style") type for more information on how styles are combined.

Note: If neither wrapping or a block is needed, consider rendering the [`Text`](../prelude/struct.Text.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Text"), [`Line`](../prelude/struct.Line.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Line"), or [`Span`](../prelude/struct.Span.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Span") widgets directly.

## [§](#example)Example

```
use ratatui::layout::Alignment;
use ratatui::style::{Style, Stylize};
use ratatui::text::{Line, Span};
use ratatui::widgets::{Block, Paragraph, Wrap};

let text = vec![
    Line::from(vec![
        Span::raw("First"),
        Span::styled("line", Style::new().green().italic()),
        ".".into(),
    ]),
    Line::from("Second line".red()),
    "Third line".into(),
];
Paragraph::new(text)
    .block(Block::bordered().title("Paragraph"))
    .style(Style::new().white().on_black())
    .alignment(Alignment::Center)
    .wrap(Wrap { trim: true });
```

