#### pub fn [line\_count](#method.line_count)(&self, width: [u16](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.u16.html)) -> [usize](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.usize.html)

Available on **crate features `unstable-rendered-line-info`** only.

Calculates the number of lines needed to fully render.

Given a max line width, this method calculates the number of lines that a paragraph will need in order to be fully rendered. For paragraphs that do not use wrapping, this count is simply the number of lines present in the paragraph.

This method will also account for the [`Block`](struct.Block.html "struct ratatui::widgets::Block") if one is set through [`Self::block`](struct.Paragraph.html#method.block "method ratatui::widgets::Paragraph::block").

Note: The design for text wrapping is not stable and might affect this API.

##### [§](#example-5)Example

[ⓘ](# "This example is not tested")

```
use ratatui::{widgets::{Paragraph, Wrap}};

let paragraph = Paragraph::new("Hello World")
    .wrap(Wrap { trim: false });
assert_eq!(paragraph.line_count(20), 1);
assert_eq!(paragraph.line_count(10), 2);
```

